  "title": "store: address review findings in SetView, VersionedStorage, createNode, FrozenNodeSet",
  "body": "Fixes the outstanding review comments on `packages/store`. Each comment first got a failing test, then the code fix.\n\n### `createNode`\n- Reads each own data property descriptor once, so a getter can no longer return different values to validation and storage.\n- Compares node-reference sets with `isSameIds`, i.e. by ID.\n\n### `SetView` (base of `FrozenSet` and `FrozenNodeSet`)\n- `difference`, `intersection`, `isDisjointFrom`, `isSubsetOf`, `isSupersetOf`, `symmetricDifference` and `union` are hand-written using only `size`/`has()`/`keys()`. They no longer depend on native `Set.prototype` methods, which are missing in Chrome/Firefox 100 and Safari 15.\n- These methods use the receiver's own `has()`, so `FrozenNodeSet` matches node references by `@id`.\n- A code comment explains why `core-js-pure` is not used:\n   - It returns its own `Set` class, so `instanceof Set` is `false`.\n   - It copies the receiver into a plain `Set`, which drops `FrozenNodeSet`'s ID matching, so `union()` duplicates references.\n\n### `VersionedStorage`: copy on move\n- A `Map` shared with older versions is never reordered.\n   - A deleted key stays in place as a `DELETED` tombstone.\n   - Re-adding a deleted key, moving a key, or piling up too many tombstones copies the head into a new `Map`.\n- An older version gets its key order by filtering its own map's keys through `has()`, and caches the result.\n- This fixes:\n   - Older snapshots changing order after a delete.\n   - Iterators exposing the head `Map` directly.\n   - Delete-then-set not moving the key to the end.\n- Replaces an earlier position-tracking fix: about 270 lines of code instead of about 420, memory per node is the same as before, and benchmarks are roughly the same.\n- Drops the `ordered: false` option; `FrozenSkipList` now uses the default storage.\n\n### Tests\n- New regression tests for each review comment, in the tests for `SetView`, `createNode`, `FrozenNodeSet`, `VersionedStorage`, `FrozenMap` and `FrozenSet`.\n- One existing `FrozenMap` expectation is corrected to insertion order (`['a', 'b', 'c']`).\n\n```ts\n// Works in browsers without native Set methods, and matches node references by ID.\nnew FrozenNodeSet(['_:m-1', '_:m-2']).union(new Set([{ '@id': '_:m-2' }, { '@id': '_:m-3' }]));\n// → _:m-1, _:m-2, _:m-3\n```",
